Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#2. The natural log hidden in the primes#2.2 The Prime Number Theorem: density $\\approx 1/\\ln(N)$ *(at [[4:18]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4PDoT7jtxmw&t=258s))*":[45,57],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#2. The natural log hidden in the primes#2.2 The Prime Number Theorem: density $\\approx 1/\\ln(N)$ *(at [[4:18]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4PDoT7jtxmw&t=258s))*#{1}":[47,57],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#2. The natural log hidden in the primes#2.3 A stranger appearance: the \"prime-power game\" *(at [[7:14]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4PDoT7jtxmw&t=434s))*":[58,73],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#2. The natural log hidden in the primes#2.3 A stranger appearance: the \"prime-power game\" *(at [[7:14]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4PDoT7jtxmw&t=434s))*#{1}":[60,73],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#3. The natural log hidden in the harmonic series":[74,121],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#3. The natural log hidden in the harmonic series#3.1 The alternating harmonic series $= \\ln 2$ *(at [[11:52]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4PDoT7jtxmw&t=712s))*":[76,86],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#3. The natural log hidden in the harmonic series#3.1 The alternating harmonic series $= \\ln 2$ *(at [[11:52]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4PDoT7jtxmw&t=712s))*#{1}":[78,86],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#3. The natural log hidden in the harmonic series#3.2 The plain harmonic series diverges — the grouping proof *(at [[13:46]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4PDoT7jtxmw&t=826s))*":[87,99],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#3. The natural log hidden in the harmonic series#3.2 The plain harmonic series diverges — the grouping proof *(at [[13:46]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4PDoT7jtxmw&t=826s))*#{1}":[89,99],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#3. The natural log hidden in the harmonic series#3.3 ...but it grows only **logarithmically** *(at [[16:58]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4PDoT7jtxmw&t=1018s))*":[100,107],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#3. The natural log hidden in the harmonic series#3.3 ...but it grows only **logarithmically** *(at [[16:58]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4PDoT7jtxmw&t=1018s))*#{1}":[102,107],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#3. The natural log hidden in the harmonic series#3.4 How slowly? When does the sum pass 1,000,000? *(at [[17:26]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4PDoT7jtxmw&t=1046s))*":[108,121],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#3. The natural log hidden in the harmonic series#3.4 How slowly? When does the sum pass 1,000,000? *(at [[17:26]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4PDoT7jtxmw&t=1046s))*#{1}":[110,121],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#4. So why is $e$ \"natural\"? — it's a convention, not magic *(at [[22:51]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4PDoT7jtxmw&t=1371s))*":[122,139],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#4. So why is $e$ \"natural\"? — it's a convention, not magic *(at [[22:51]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4PDoT7jtxmw&t=1371s))*#{1}":[124,139],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#Key takeaways":[140,148],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#Key takeaways#{1}":[142,142],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#Key takeaways#{2}":[143,143],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#Key takeaways#{3}":[144,144],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#Key takeaways#{4}":[145,146],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#Key takeaways#{5}":[147,148],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#Related Documents":[149,160],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#Related Documents#{1}":[151,152],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#Related Documents#{2}":[153,154],"#The Natural Logarithm — Why Is It \"Natural\"?#Related Documents#Sources":[155